// a `const` array reads and does not write, which is the whole of what `const` means on one. the
// read is pinned by arrays/const_array_read; these are the two shapes that still refuse, and they
// refuse for different reasons - one is the storage, the other is the method
Array<int32> $source = [1, 2];
const $frozen = $source;

// the element contract a const array reaches hands back `const T&`, so the storage this names is
// const - refused as a const violation rather than as a failed conversion to `Array<int32>&`
$frozen[0] = 5;

// and a method that did not declare itself a reader is refused by name, with the modifier that
// would fix it
$frozen->push(3);
